Avo ships twenty built-in themes (lib/avo/builtin_themes.rb). Thirteen of them
reuse color palettes from code editor themes, under their licenses, one theme
per published variant (Solarized Light and Solarized Dark, and so on). The
names are used descriptively, to identify the palette.

- Monokai — palette by Wimer Hazenberg (2006). The classic values are reused;
  this is not Monokai Pro.
- Dracula — Zeno Rocha and contributors, MIT. https://draculatheme.com
- Solarized — Ethan Schoonover, MIT. https://ethanschoonover.com/solarized
- Nord — Sven Greb and contributors, MIT. https://www.nordtheme.com
- Gruvbox — Pavel Pertsev and contributors, MIT. https://github.com/morhetz/gruvbox
- One Dark / One Light — the Atom team, MIT. https://github.com/atom/one-dark-syntax
- Catppuccin — the Catppuccin organization, MIT. https://catppuccin.com
- Tokyo Night — Enrico Kaiser (enkia), MIT. https://github.com/enkia/tokyo-night-vscode-theme

